From 2b3388b95da2cee2db5476b2517aebbec1820bae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:03:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 443/453] fix(desktop): reuse remote SSH backends across quit
 and reconnect (W0) [daveey]

Opening a session on a remote gateway cost 6-10 s (cloud) to ~19 s (Mac)
before the first request, because almost every connection spawned a fresh
`serve --isolated`: every teardown, including quit, sleep-resume and tunnel
rebuilds, killed the owned backend (cleanupStale), so the persisted reuse
token never found a live backend.

- ssh-teardown-policy.ts: a teardown reason decides the remote action.
  quit, bootstrap-retry, revalidate, resume and idle-stop RELEASE the
  backend (tunnel and SSH close; backend and lockfile stay). Deliberate
  changes (fingerprint change, removed connection, recycle, config apply,
  profile teardown) and any unlisted reason TERMINATE, as before. Windows
  remotes are skipped, as before.
- The reason travels through pool stops (stopPoolBackend / stopAllPoolBackends
  -> afterStop) so quit and resume no longer terminate via the pool path;
  uninstall and the Windows update stop still terminate.
- remote-lifecycle: release() keeps an owned backend and its lockfile and
  fails closed on skewed records; connect() logs `reuse miss: <reasons>`
  for every present-but-unreused backend.

The leak bound stays: a released backend exits on its own 900 s after its
last client and never mid-turn (web_server_idle_exit.py), one per host and
ownership id (lockfile). The adopted token was already persisted encrypted.

Tests: remote-lifecycle-release.test.ts (release keeps backend and lock;
fails closed on skew; reconnect after release reuses with the persisted
token; exact miss reasons logged; teardown policy table). Related suites:
292 passed; the 7 failures are identical on the base (environment).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 2b3388b95da2cee2db5476b2517aebbec1820bae)
